Summary: Create README with setup and security notes for agent

Reasoning:
Action: FileEditorAction

Arguments:
  command: "create"
  path: "/workspace/README_MONITOR.md"
  file_text: 
    Monitor Agent (temporary)
    
    This small agent is designed for short-term troubleshooting in the staging environment.
    
    Files created:
    - /workspace/monitor_agent.py  - main agent script
    - /workspace/requirements.txt  - python dependencies
    - /workspace/run_monitor.sh    - simple nohup launcher (creates /workspace/monitor_agent.pid)
    - /workspace/monitor_agent.service - optional systemd unit file
    - /workspace/monitor_agent.log - runtime log
    - /workspace/debug_token      - secret token for debug exec endpoint (created automatically)
    
    What it does
    - Exposes Prometheus-compatible metrics on /metrics (default port 9091)
    - Collects CPU, memory, disk, load average, process count
    - Optional HTTP checks if you set CHECK_URLS environment variable
    - Provides a small debug HTTP endpoint on /exec (default port 9092) which accepts JSON POST payloads 
with a token to execute commands and returns stdout/stderr
    - Provides /logs and /health endpoints for quick checks
    
    Security and usage notes
    - By default the agent binds to 127.0.0.1. If you need remote access, prefer creating an SSH tunnel 
to the debug port instead of binding to 0.0.0.0.
    - The debug exec endpoint can run arbitrary commands; the token is written to /workspace/debug_token.
Keep that file secure.
    - You can restrict which commands are allowed by setting ALLOWED_CMDS (comma-separated list). If 
unset, all commands are allowed.
    
    Quick start
    1) Install dependencies:
       pip3 install -r /workspace/requirements.txt
    
    2) Start the agent in background:
       /workspace/run_monitor.sh
    
       or run directly (foreground):
       python3 /workspace/monitor_agent.py
    
    3) Metrics will be available at:
       http://<host>:9091/metrics
    
    4) Debug endpoints (default on localhost:9092):
       - POST /exec  with JSON {"token":"<token>", "cmd":"ls -la"}
       - GET /logs?lines=200
       - GET /health
    
    Retrieve the debug token:
       cat /workspace/debug_token
    
    Systemd (optional)
    - Copy /workspace/monitor_agent.service to /etc/systemd/system/ then enable/start:
      sudo cp /workspace/monitor_agent.service /etc/systemd/system/
      sudo systemctl daemon-reload
      sudo systemctl enable --now monitor_agent.service
    
    If you need me to bind the debug endpoint to a public interface or install a monitoring scrape 
configuration in Prometheus, I can make that change—but be aware of the security implications.
    

