  then curl POST to http://127.0.0.1:9092/exec
- If you still want a raw netcat listener on a high port, I recommend a wrapped approach (token check or 
SSH reverse tunnel) instead of an unauthenticated netcat shell. I can:
  1) Enable binding the debug endpoint to 0.0.0.0 (set BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0) — less secure.
  2) Add a simple token gate for a raw netcat-style listener — safer but still risky.
  3) Configure socat with TLS or an SSH reverse tunnel for secure remote shells.

