     1  Monitor Agent (temporary)
     2  
     3  This small agent is designed for short-term troubleshooting in the staging environment.
     4  
     5  Files created:
     6  - /workspace/monitor_agent.py  - main agent script
     7  - /workspace/requirements.txt  - python dependencies
     8  - /workspace/run_monitor.sh    - simple nohup launcher (creates /workspace/monitor_agent.pid)
     9  - /workspace/monitor_agent.service - optional systemd unit file
    10  - /workspace/monitor_agent.log - runtime log
    11  - /workspace/debug_token      - secret token for debug exec endpoint (created automatically)
    12  
    13  What it does
    14  - Exposes Prometheus-compatible metrics on /metrics (default port 9091)
    15  - Collects CPU, memory, disk, load average, process count
    16  - Optional HTTP checks if you set CHECK_URLS environment variable
    17  - Provides a small debug HTTP endpoint on /exec (default port 9092) which accepts JSON POST 
payloads with a token to execute commands and returns stdout/stderr
    18  - Provides /logs and /health endpoints for quick checks
    19  
    20  Security and usage notes
    21  - By default the agent binds to 127.0.0.1. If you need remote access, prefer creating an SSH 
tunnel to the debug port instead of binding to 0.0.0.0.
    22  - The debug exec endpoint can run arbitrary commands; the token is written to 
/workspace/debug_token. Keep that file secure.
    23  - You can restrict which commands are allowed by setting ALLOWED_CMDS (comma-separated list). If 
unset, all commands are allowed.
    24  
    25  Quick start
    26  1) Install dependencies:
    27     pip3 install -r /workspace/requirements.txt
    28  
    29  2) Start the agent in background:
    30     /workspace/run_monitor.sh
    31  
    32     or run directly (foreground):
    33     python3 /workspace/monitor_agent.py
    34  
    35  3) Metrics will be available at:
    36     http://<host>:9091/metrics
    37  
    38  4) Debug endpoints (default on localhost:9092):
    39     - POST /exec  with JSON {"token":"<token>", "cmd":"ls -la"}
    40     - GET /logs?lines=200
    41     - GET /health
    42  
    43  Retrieve the debug token:
    44     cat /workspace/debug_token
    45  
    46  Systemd (optional)
    47  - Copy /workspace/monitor_agent.service to /etc/systemd/system/ then enable/start:
    48    sudo cp /workspace/monitor_agent.service /etc/systemd/system/
    49    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    50    sudo systemctl enable --now monitor_agent.service
    51  
