Summary: Append alerting and persistence instructions to README_MONITOR.md

Action: FileEditorAction

Arguments:
  command: "insert"
  path: "/workspace/README_MONITOR.md"
  new_str: 
    
    Alerting and persistence
    - A lightweight alert agent is available at /workspace/alert_agent.py. Configure via environment 
variables:
      - ALERT_INTERVAL, CPU_THRESHOLD, MEM_THRESHOLD, DISK_THRESHOLD, ROCKETCHAT_WEBHOOK, ALERT_THROTTLE
      - Example (runs once in background):
          ROCKETCHAT_WEBHOOK="https://your-rocketchat/hooks/xyz" /workspace/start_all.sh
    - For systems without systemd, a simple supervisor script is provided:
      - /workspace/start_all.sh (starts monitor_agent, log_streamer, token_shell, token_shell_tls, 
alert_agent)
      - /workspace/stop_all.sh (stops services using pidfiles)
    
    TLS token shell notes
    - A TLS-protected token shell is available at /workspace/token_shell_tls.py. It creates a self-signed
cert at /workspace/token_shell.crt and /workspace/token_shell.key.
    - To connect: use openssl s_client or socat, then paste token from /workspace/debug_token as the 
first line.
    
    Security
    - If exposing the TLS shell publicly, restrict access with firewall rules or IP allow-lists and 
rotate the token regularly.
    - Prefer SSH tunnels (ssh -L) for interactive debugging when possible.
    

